  "query_preview": "..\nThe proximity to the monsoon trough will continue to produce regional\ninstability, allowing scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms to\ncontinue into the evening. Showers and thunder will taper down coming\ninto Saturday morning, with island showers returning near noon as\nwinds remain light and variable. Invest 93W, now a sub-low and \nlocated over the northern Marshalls, is expected to continue on its\njourney toward the Marianas and eventually break down into an open\ntrough, with some chance to bring just low-end scattered showers to\nthe area in the first half of next week. \n\nMarine...\nCombined seas of 3 to 4 feet are expected for much of the forecast \nperiod, as various swells from the west and east remain weak. Due to\nthese weak swells, a low risk of rip currents is expected along all\nreefs of the Marianas for at least the next several days.\n\nEastern Micronesia...\nThe main weather theme will be a continued unsettled pattern \ncontinuing as we head through the weekend and into next week. In \ngeneral, a monsoon trough bisects the area, stretching from Pohnpei \nto south of Majuro, connecting to a broad/weak circulation near \n7N177E, before crossing the Date Line near 8N180. The circulation \neast of Majuro, and another one further east near 9N170W, looks to \ncontinue west over the next several days. While this occurs, a \npersistent west-southwest monsoon flow will continue. This allows \nthe trough to act as a good convergence boundary, allowing scattered \nshowers and isolated thunderstorms to develop. The previous forecasts\nhad this well in hand and we continued that theme this afternoon, \nnudging rainfall probabilities up, just slightly. \n\nWinds will generally be light to gentle at Kosrae and Majuro, with \ngeneral to moderate winds at Pohnpei decreasing back into the light \nto gentle range over the weekend. Seas of 3 to 5 feet will also \npersist through the forecast period.\n\nWestern Micronesia...\nWet weather will continue at Chuuk and Yap as surface convergence\nin the vicinity of the monsoon trough brings periods of scattered to\nlow-end numerous showers and isolated thunderstorms to both \nlocations through the weekend. Drier weather is expected at Palau \nthrough Saturday with shower chances increasing starting Sunday. \n\nLight to moderate west to northwest winds will continue through the\nweekend at Palau and Yap with the strongest winds being at Yap \nthrough Saturday. West to southwest gentle to moderate winds will \ncontinue at Chuuk through Sunday. Generally benign marine conditions \nwill persist through the weekend at all forecast points with combined\nseas hovering around 3 to 4 feet.",
